meta {
  name: Get Order
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Fetch one order fully composed: patient ref, active `items` (with their resolved
  test/panel and the per-line `discount`), the `diagnostics`/`opd`/`radiology`
  sections with resolved refs, and the active `payments` ledger. Also returns
  `orderTime` and the `billingDetails` sub-form. 404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` if missing,
  soft-deleted, or owned by another tenant.

  Each item's `unitPrice` is the authoritative per-line price — the amount
  actually resolved/charged at order or quotation time (from the pricing list's
  `listPrice` for a catalogue line, or the client-supplied amount for a `direct`
  line — see "Create Order"). This is the field to render/edit as the line's
  price. The nested `branchLabTest.priceMsrp`/`branchLabPanel.priceMsrp` is a
  **different** field — the referenced catalogue's current master reference
  price, which is independently editable in Master Data and may have since
  drifted from what this line was actually charged. Do not use `priceMsrp` for
  line pricing/totals.

  Also returns `hasInvoice` (boolean) and `invoiceCode` (the linked invoice's
  number, or null): true when an invoice has been generated for this order (an
  active `InvoiceSourceOrder` link exists). An invoiced order is locked — it can
  no longer be updated (`PATCH /orders/:id`) or cancelled (`PATCH
  /orders/:id/cancel`); both return 409 `ORDER_ALREADY_INVOICED`. Cancelling the
  invoice unlinks it and returns `hasInvoice` to false.
}
